# NOTE: .Rbuildignore has no real comment syntax -- R compiles every
# non-blank line (# lines included) as its own Perl regex and matches it
# against relative file paths. A "#" line is normally a harmless no-op
# (matches nothing), EXCEPT R CMD build hard-errors if that line isn't
# valid regex on its own -- confirmed the hard way: a multi-line comment
# here with an opening "(" on one line and its closing ")" on the next
# broke the regex compiler and failed every subsequent build, including
# the one that shipped changelog.md into a real released tarball because
# the (broken) exclusion for it silently never took effect. Keep every
# comment line below self-contained and free of unbalanced regex
# metacharacters -- no line-spanning parens/brackets/quotes.
^examples$
# _extensions: repo-root physical copy of inst/extensions/quartifyr/,
# kept in sync by scripts/sync_demo_extension.py, that exists solely so
# `quarto add jprybylski/quartifyr` finds a valid extension (issue #16).
# Not part of the R package -- the package installs from
# inst/extensions/quartifyr/ via install_quartifyr_extension().
^_extensions$
^docs$
^scripts$
^tests/python$
^\.github$
^\.venv$
^\.githooks$
^uv\.lock$
^pyproject\.toml$
^CONTRIBUTING\.md$
^CLAUDE\.md$
^action\.yml$
^VERSION$
# changelog.md: scratch file sync-release-metadata.R writes just before
# R CMD build runs in the same release.yaml job; not meant to ship.
^changelog\.md$
# LICENSE: DESCRIPTION's License field (GPL (>= 3)) doesn't reference the
# file form, so R CMD check flags it as unmentioned (issue #62). Excluded
# rather than switching to "GPL-3 + file LICENSE", which isn't what was
# asked and would change the License field's meaning.
^LICENSE$
# man/figures/*.gif and the two examples' downloadable final .docx files:
# pkgdown-site-only assets demo GIFs and real rendered output for download,
# see scripts/render_doc_screenshots.py, that no .Rd's figure tag
# references, confirmed by grep, and that made up most of this package's
# ~4.8MB tarball, issue #62, not needed by the installed R package
# itself. man/figures/*.png stays, small, and README.md's logo.png is
# GitHub/pkgdown-rendered, not roxygen-referenced, but harmless to keep.
^man/figures/.*\.gif$
^man/figures/demo-report-final\.docx$
^man/figures/memo-example-final\.docx$
^\.Rhistory$
^\.claude$
^\.pytest_cache$
^\.rpfy-logs$
^dev$
^_pkgdown\.yml$
^pkgdown$
^logo-files$
# vignettes/articles/: pkgdown's own "article, not a real vignette" path.
# Site-only content, not a package vignette, no VignetteBuilder needed.
^vignettes/articles$
